{#
  headlamp's verify Job and the ConfigMap that carries its script.

  The manifests role takes only top-level `templates/*.yaml.j2`, and `verify_files` takes only
  `templates/verify/*.yaml.j2`, so the renderer emits this directory into `headlamp-verify` (D5,
  *A verify conversion lands as inert code*). It replaced the `headlamp-netpol-probe` Job, whose
  tasks and `netpol-probe-job.yaml.j2` the flip deleted.

  Both names end in a digest, as the Job census requires (D5, *Rules for every Job Flux
  applies*): the ConfigMap's in `configmap_digest8` of its data, the Job's in
  `job_spec_digest8` of its spec. Each is computed here from the same JSON those functions
  hash, so the spec is written once as YAML text, parsed for the hash and emitted verbatim.
  The renderer passes `flux_job_image` and `flux_job_connect`, the helper's text, to every
  `templates/verify/` file (`render_tag`).

  The spec embeds a digest of headlamp's rendered NetworkPolicy and Deployment. The fence is
  what this Job tests, so an edit to `networkpolicy.yaml.j2` alone renames the Job and makes
  Flux run it again. The Deployment is in the digest because a roll replaces the pod the
  policy selects.

  The caller census (D5, *A fence admits every Job that dials through it*). The pod is
  `app: headlamp-verify` in `k8s_namespace`, and it dials two ports and execs into nothing:
    - traefik:80, the control. netpol-baseline's `networkpolicy-traefik.yaml.j2` opens
      traefik's web port with a rule that names no `from`, so every pod reaches it and no
      peer is added. The port is a literal because traefik's defaults do not resolve in this
      role; the probe this Job replaces dials the same literal. If that rule narrowed, the
      control would be refused and the Job would fail closed;
    - headlamp:<port>. `networkpolicy.yaml.j2` must REFUSE this pod, so no peer is added to
      headlamp's `netpol_from`: admitting `headlamp-verify` would open the hole the Job
      proves closed. ansible/roles/k8s/headlamp/tests/test_headlamp_verify.py fails if that
      fence admits the label.
#}
{% set script_name = 'headlamp_verify.py' %}
{% set script_dir = '/verify' %}
{% set data = {
  script_name: lookup('file', playbook_dir + '/roles/k8s/headlamp/files/' + script_name, rstrip=False),
  'flux_job_connect.py': flux_job_connect,
} %}
{% set configmap_name = 'headlamp-verify-' + ({'data': data, 'binaryData': {}} | to_json(sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] %}
{% set render_digest8 = ((lookup('template', 'networkpolicy.yaml.j2') + lookup('template', 'deployment.yaml.j2')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] %}
{% set spec_text %}
# A flaky check fails rather than passing on a retry.
backoffLimit: 0
# Below the 600s `manifests_rollout_timeout_default` every `<tag>-verify` Kustomization takes.
# The control's 60s of connect retries, then one 5s connect.
activeDeadlineSeconds: 180
template:
  metadata:
    labels:
      # No peer of headlamp's fence, which is what the isolation leg needs. It must never be
      # `traefik`.
      app: headlamp-verify
  spec:
    serviceAccountName: headlamp-verify
    # The Job reads no Kubernetes API, so its pod holds no token.
    automountServiceAccountToken: false
    restartPolicy: Never
    enableServiceLinks: false
    securityContext:
      runAsNonRoot: true
      runAsUser: 65534
      runAsGroup: 65534
      seccompProfile:
        type: RuntimeDefault
    containers:
      - name: verify
        image: {{ flux_job_image }}
        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
        command:
          - python3
          - {{ script_dir }}/{{ script_name }}
        env:
          - name: CONTROL_URL
            value: http://traefik.{{ k8s_namespace }}.svc.cluster.local:80/
          - name: HEADLAMP_URL
            value: http://{{ container_item.name }}.{{ k8s_namespace }}.svc.cluster.local:{{ container_item.port }}/
          # Renames the Job whenever headlamp's policy or Deployment changes; see the note above.
          - name: HEADLAMP_RENDER_DIGEST8
            value: "{{ render_digest8 }}"
          - name: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE
            value: "1"
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: 10m
            memory: 32Mi
          limits:
            memory: 64Mi
        securityContext:
          allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
          readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
          capabilities:
            drop:
              - ALL
        volumeMounts:
          - name: script
            mountPath: {{ script_dir }}
            readOnly: true
    volumes:
      - name: script
        configMap:
          name: {{ configmap_name }}
{% endset %}
{% set spec = spec_text | from_yaml %}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ configmap_name }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
data:
{% for key, text in data | dictsort %}
  {{ key }}: {{ text | to_json }}
{% endfor %}
---
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: headlamp-verify-{{ (spec | to_json(sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')) | hash('sha256'))[:8] }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
  annotations:
    homelab/job-kind: verify
spec:
{{ spec_text | indent(2, true) }}
